# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-12, R-3, RC-6). L §3.6 The arrival rule, What it may read: "parts as they stood at the start
# of the arrival's day or earlier (bal(y, m.day start) of q), so income from a co-owned asset can follow its owners'
# parts. The walk runs it when it books the arrival, so these are the walk's reads (§5.14.1); a read at the end of the
# arrival's day or later is a cycle with the booking (LOAD-CYCLE)"; L §5.14.1 The arrival rule is a reader too: "The
# start of the arrival's day is booked before anything that day, so reading it is no cycle; a read of the end of the
# arrival's day or later is (LOAD-CYCLE where load sees the day, RUN-CYCLE otherwise)".
# i1's interest follows dep's parts at the start of its day: ania 300.00, tomek 100.00, so 30.00 and 10.00
# (scratch/exp5.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w prorata
kind interests: transfers
kind tomeks: transfers
input k0: int
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place dep: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
input i1_day: date
input i1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
  rule income beats base, t = bal(dep, m.day start) of p / bal(dep, m.day start) when m in interests
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to dep amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to dep amount t1_amt
move i1: interests
  on i1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount i1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, k0

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[dep] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 300.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  i1_day = 2026-03-01
  i1_amt = 40.00 PLN
  k0 = 0
=== expect
q: (30.00 PLN, 10.00 PLN, 0)
  cut 2026-01-01
